    creditLine:
      "Bequest of Richard De Wolfe Brixey, 1943\r\n\r\nThis work has been deaccessioned because it is redundant of more significant examples of Gilbert Stuart’s portrayal of Washington as well as other contemporaneous portraits of him by various leading artists in the Museum’s collection.\r\n\r\nIn accordance with the Museum’s policy, due to the value of the work (over $50,000) and the fact that it has been on exhibition in the Museum in the preceding ten years, public notice is being given that the Museum plans to dispose of the work via public auction.  If you have comments on the Museum’s plan to dispose of the work, please send them to deaccessioning@metmuseum.org.",
